          %h3#for_monopole_charges_in_electromagnetism For monopole charges in electromagnetism
          %p
            If the field of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetism"} electromagnetism
            serves as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+gauge+field"} background gauge field
            for electrically charged
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/particles"} particles
            it is subject to a
            = succeed ":" do
              %em quantization condition
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+charge"} magnetic charge
            – for instance a magnetic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monopole"} monopole
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+defect"} topological defect
            – the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
            must be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+bundle+with+connection"} connection on a principal U(1) bundle
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
            is the discrete measure for the units of magnetic charge. Equivalently this means that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            of degree 2.
          %p
            In the underlying topological sector (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monopole"}> monopole
            ”/“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instantons"}> instantons
            ”-sector) this is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+cohomology"} integral cohomology
            in degree-2, whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            is equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+complex+projective+space"} infinite complex projective space
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B U(1) \simeq \mathbb{C}P^\infty
          %p#Illustration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/DiracChargeQuantizationII.jpg", :width => "640"}/
          %p
            This goes back to an insight due to
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Dirac31"} Dirac 31
            %a{:href => "#Heras18"} Heras 18
            for traditional elementary review, but see
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Alvarez85"} Alvarez 85
            %a{:href => "#Frankel"} Frankel
            and
            %a{:href => "#MangiarottiSardanashvily00"} Mangiarotti-Sardanashvily 00
            for exposition of the modern picture in terms of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundles+in+physics"} fiber bundles in physics
            %a{:href => "#Freed00"} Freed 00, Section 2
            for review in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            with outlook to generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+fields"} higher gauge fields
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            (more on which in the references
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#ReferencesForBFieldAndRRFields"} below
          %p
            A closely related phenomenon is the magnetic flux quantization in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+superconductors"} type II superconductors
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "superconductivity#MagneticFluxQuantizationInTypeIISuperconductors"} there
          %p
            On the locus of the magnetic charge itself the situation is more complex. There the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+current"} magnetic current
            is given by a cocycle in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            of degree 3 (with compact support) and now the electromagnetic field is a connection on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+bundle"} twisted bundle
            (
            %a{:href => "#Freed00"}> Freed 00, Section 2
            ).
          %p
            %br/
          %h3#for_monopole_charges_in_nonabelian_yangmills_theory For monopole charges in non-abelian Yang-Mills theory
          %p
            A similar charge quantization condition govers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monopoles"} monopoles
            in
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SU%282%29"} SU(2)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+monopoles"} moduli space of monopoles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah-Hitchin+charge+quantization"} Atiyah-Hitchin charge quantization
            (
            %a{:href => "#AtiyahHitchin88"}> Atiyah-Hitchin 88, Theorem 2.10
            ) says that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monopoles"} monopoles
            is the
            = succeed "-" do
